  "_doc": "Rover and robot builder (src/rover/rover_design.gd). A design is one chassis plus parts. Parts with a 'payload' id are the payload planner's own modules (data/tycoon/payload.json: their mass, power, gen, store and cost come from there, so the rover and the planner agree); the others (chassis, arm, drone, weather station, sample cache) are the rover's own and travel in the plan as one 'rover:' payload module (RoverDesign.payload_code). 'option' needs that research option (unlocked['option:<id>']), 'tech' that research tech (unlocked[<tech>]). 'tool' is the surface action the part gives (SurfaceSession.ACTIONS). 'mounts' are the chassis' Marker3D names it can sit on, first free wins. 'scene' is the editor-authored voxel part (scenes/rover/parts/). 'step' is the tallest rise the chassis drives over (m), 'clearance' the belly height above its wheels' contact (m). Units: kg, W, Wh, cr, m/s, degrees. Texts: RV_PART_<ID> / RV_PART_<ID>_DESC in i18n/rover_strings.csv.",
