  "_bodies": "Surface facts the rover reads: sun (sunlight on the panels vs the Moon), air (an atmosphere a drone can fly in), delay_s (one-way radio delay to Earth, s; Mars is minutes), night (does a night fall during a drive).",
  "bodies": {
    "earth":   {"sun": 1.0,  "air": true,  "delay_s": 0.05},
    "moon":    {"sun": 1.0,  "air": false, "delay_s": 1.3},
    "mars":    {"sun": 0.43, "air": true,  "delay_s": 750.0},
    "mercury": {"sun": 6.7,  "air": false, "delay_s": 400.0},
    "europa":  {"sun": 0.04, "air": false, "delay_s": 2600.0},
    "titan":   {"sun": 0.011, "air": true, "delay_s": 4800.0}
  },
  "_rules": "range_km: how far the battery (plus a sunny day) drives before it must stop and recharge, a plain-language estimate: (store + gen * day_h) / drive power * speed. science: the sum of the instruments' science x 1 + 0.15 per extra tool. A design must have one chassis, a power source that runs it (gen or a battery), an antenna, at most 'bays' instruments and 'power_bays' power parts.",
  "rules": {"instrument_idle": 0.1, "day_h": 6.0, "min_tools_for_bonus": 2, "tool_bonus": 0.15, "idle_power": 4.0},
  "starter": {"name_key": "RV_STARTER_NAME", "chassis": "wheels4", "parts": ["solar", "battery", "camera", "beacon"]}
